"""Original teaching and delivery copy. One record per published lab timebox."""

def track(title,steps,notes,gate,proof,rescue,gate_notes):
    return dict(title=title,steps=steps,notes=notes,gate=gate,proof=proof,rescue=rescue,gate_notes=gate_notes)

LABS=[
dict(short='Establish the baseline',range='00–08',min=8,
 a=track('Start in the app, not the repository',[
 ('Open the starter folder','In VS Code, open workshop/Advanced/sampleapp. Its .github folder must be at the workspace root.'),
 ('Test before editing','Run node --version, then node --check src/server.js and node --test. Use Node.js 22 or newer.'),
 ('Prepare the session','Choose Copilot Agent mode and an available workshop model. Keep instructor-issued connection details out of chat.')],
 'The starter already parses sessions, reconstructs file edits and serves a browser UI. A clean test run makes it possible to distinguish a starter problem from a regression you introduce later.',
 'What can you reproduce before editing?',
 'Show your workspace root, the Node version and a test run with zero failures. The manifest needs no dependencies or devDependencies.',
 'If tests are missing, check the terminal folder. If syntax fails, check Node first. Do not install packages to hide a baseline failure.',
 'Keep the first failure message if you need help. You do not need any service credentials to test the baseline.'),
 p=track('Set up a baseline the room can trust',[
 ('First 3 min  /  orient the room','Open the app folder directly. Show the local parser, native HTTP server and package-free manifest before changing anything.'),
 ('Next 2 min  /  check the harness','Ask one learner to show the Agent picker. Use an available approved model; do not wait for everyone to find the same model name.'),
 ('Final 3 min  /  establish privacy','Name the five connection fields without projecting their values. Use only approved synthetic sessions throughout the demos.')],
 'Run the baseline commands in the app root while participants open their terminals. Explain that Chronicle reads saved sessions; it does not need to edit the original histories. Keep connection material entirely off the shared screen.',
 'Take a baseline reading at minute 8',
 'Ask a pair to show node --test with zero failures and identify the folder containing .github/copilot-instructions.md.',
 'If discovery or tests fail for several people, compare their Explorer roots. Pair an unblocked learner with a neighbor rather than starting a package install.',
 'Ask: what can we prove today without Foundry? The parser, browser, manifest invariant and mocked service routes are all local checks.'),
 screen=('starter',
 ('Introduce the starter with a safe fixture','DEMO CUE','Open session → select practice-session.jsonl from content/assets.','Ask what a teammate would lose if given only the last assistant reply.','Use “Verify the route migration” as the synthetic reference. Do not browse a participant’s actual session library. The captured route-test command is historical fixture data, not a command to run in Chronicle.'),
 ('Find the reader you must preserve','STARTER SCREEN','Open session → select practice-session.jsonl from content/assets.','Find “Verify the route migration.” What did the test establish, and what remains to be done?','Read full session is a reading action. In the fixture both route versions passed; updating the sample client remains open. The summary feature should preserve this distinction.')),
 recap='Baseline recap: a clean start needs Node and a browser, not a package install.'),

dict(short='Design the agent team',range='08–25',min=17,
 a=track('Give five agents distinct responsibilities',[
 ('Create the four worker profiles','Under .github/agents, create chronicle-dev, chronicle-test, chronicle-security and chronicle-docs files ending in .agent.md.'),
 ('Create chronicle-orchestrator.agent.md','Give the lead read, search, agent and todo tools. Set user-invocable: true for the lead and false for workers.'),
 ('Inspect the handoff contract','In Chat: Open Customizations, check all five profiles. Assign one writer per file; ask for a changed path and a test or finding in each report.')],
 'Use default Agent mode to create the profiles. Developer owns src/ and public/; Tester owns test/; Documentation owns guide files. Security can read and search, not edit. The lead returns a failed gate to the right owner for remediation.',
 'Who can change a failed implementation?',
 'Five profiles are discovered. The lead can delegate but cannot edit. Security cites a file and line; Developer fixes it; Tester reruns the check.',
 'If workers clutter the picker, check user-invocable. If the lead cannot dispatch, inspect the agent tool and worker invocation settings.',
 'Check names exactly as shown in your workspace. For a worker to remain callable by the lead, do not disable model invocation. Inspect YAML warnings before continuing.'),
 p=track('Teach delegation as a permission decision',[
 ('10 min  /  build the four workers','Contrast Security’s read/search tools with Developer’s edit/execute tools. Ask who owns tests and who may change the README.'),
 ('5 min  /  remove tools from the lead','Create Chronicle Orchestrator without edit or execute. Ask it to plan a change with file ownership and a measurable acceptance check.'),
 ('2 min  /  trace a failed review','Use Chat: Open Customizations to inspect five profiles. Have the group route a security finding back to Developer, then to Tester.')],
 'A single conversation can mingle code, test output and policy. Delegation helps only if the result crossing each boundary is small and verifiable. Model a handoff: “Own public/app.js; preserve the reader; return changed paths and a browser check.”',
 'Ask for the rerun, not just the fix',
 'A learner can trace the report from read-only Security to the lead, to Developer for a fix, and back to Tester for fresh evidence.',
 'If a worker is missing, inspect workspace scope and YAML diagnostics. Do not grant edit to the lead as a shortcut.',
 'Show the difference between five workspace profiles in Customizations and one user-invocable custom lead in the picker. Keep the default built-in agents out of the count.'),
 diagram=('One entry point, four narrower jobs','Trace a single request down the branches. Developer implements; Tester adds independent checks; Security reports findings without edits; Documentation records the interface. When evidence fails, the lead reopens the implementation task.',
 [('Developer','source + UI'),('Tester','tests + results'),('Security','file:line findings'),('Documentation','guides + prompts')],
 'Ask: if the audit fails, who is allowed to change the source?',
 'Give each worker an owned path, an acceptance check and a result to return.'),
 recap='Agent recap: tool permissions enforce the separation that role names only describe.'),

dict(short='Write reusable skills',range='25–40',min=15,
 a=track('Turn a repeated procedure into a skill',[
 ('Create four SKILL.md files','Put each file in .github/skills/<name>/. Match the YAML name to its directory. Write a description that says when to use it.'),
 ('Write a testable procedure','For the test skill: bind node:http mocks to 127.0.0.1 on port 0. Test READY, denied auth and redaction when an upstream error echoes a fake token.'),
 ('Make the role-to-skill link explicit','Reference the matching SKILL.md path in the worker instructions. In a new chat, select Chronicle Orchestrator and ask for the test plan.')],
 'A role defines tools and instructions. A skill packages a workflow and is discovered by its description. Do not depend on a skills frontmatter field being supported by every harness. Confirm the worker used the intended procedure by inspecting its plan.',
 'Did the worker use the procedure?',
 'Find four skills in workspace customizations. Ask Tester how it will prove a fake secret is absent on failure. Expect a local mock and an explicit negative assertion.',
 'If discovery fails, check SKILL.md capitalization, directory/name agreement and description. Point the worker directly to the skill file.',
 'A listed skill is not proof of use. Compare the returned plan with its body. If the plan proposes a live service or external package, ask for the local built-in alternative.'),
 p=track('Make skill discovery observable',[
 ('10 min  /  author a useful trigger','Contrast “testing” with “use when checking Foundry OAuth failures against a loopback mock.” Ask what evidence the second workflow produces.'),
 ('3 min  /  connect procedure to role','Have each worker reference its own SKILL.md path. Roles set permissions; a skill supplies a repeatable method, not extra tools.'),
 ('2 min  /  observe selection','Use a new chat with Chronicle Orchestrator. Delegate a mock test plan; look for a loopback listener, a fake token and a redaction assertion.')],
 'Anchor the explanation in a concrete case: a happy-path READY response says nothing about secret handling on failure. The test skill makes that negative case reproducible. Skill discovery is description-based; support for preload metadata varies by harness.',
 'Distinguish discovery from execution',
 'Ask the room to name the trigger and the expected output. Accept a worker plan that follows its role-specific procedure, not just a visible skill name.',
 'If preload metadata is unrecognized, remove reliance on it. Put the exact matching SKILL.md path in the worker body and repeat the task.',
 'If time is tight, inspect one role-to-skill mapping aloud and have pairs verify the other three. Do not imply the same YAML field preloads skills on every agent surface.'),
 diagram=('Four procedures worth keeping','Read each pair as a reusable method, not as a tool grant. Developer uses built-ins and atomic writes; Tester mocks auth and responses; Security audits boundaries; Documentation specifies setup and a portable handoff.',
 [('Developer','zero-package-engineering'),('Tester','foundry-oauth-testing'),('Security','local-app-security-audit'),('Documentation','foundry-handoff-docs')],
 'Ask which procedure should catch a token echoed by a failed upstream request.',
 'Example path: .github/skills/foundry-oauth-testing/SKILL.md'),
 recap='Skill recap: the agent defines who may act; the skill describes how to do the job.'),

dict(short='Configure Foundry',range='40–55',min=15,
 a=track('Keep credentials on the server side',[
 ('Delegate the config route and docs','Ask the lead for GET/POST /api/summary/config and POST /api/summary/test. Put setup and the three agent prompt modes in agentconfig/.'),
 ('Persist locally and return less','Write ignored .env atomically. A blank secret on update preserves the saved value. GET returns hasClientSecret, never the secret itself.'),
 ('Exercise both hops','With approved workshop access, save the five fields in Summary agent and test. Entra issues a token; Foundry answers the connection probe with READY.')],
 'The five inputs are tenant ID, client ID, client secret, agent endpoint and agent name. Output defaults to summaries. Use built-in fetch with client_credentials and scope https://ai.azure.com/.default. Require HTTPS except for local mock listeners.',
 'Does “configured” mean “connected”?',
 'No. A saved form proves storage. A live READY reply with auth and agent timings proves the two-hop check. Mock responses prove only local behavior.',
 'If auth fails, check tenant, client and secret privately. If auth succeeds but the agent denies access, check endpoint, name and role assignment. Use mocks if blocked.',
 'Check the public config after save and after a blank-secret update. Inspect a fake upstream failure: neither secret nor bearer token may appear in the UI or copied log. Do not paste live diagnostics into chat.'),
 p=track('Separate a saved form from a verified call',[
 ('10 min  /  dispatch implementation','Assign config routes and dialog to Developer; give Documentation the portal setup guide and prompts for connection, chunk digest and final summary.'),
 ('Require independent checks','Tester mocks both HTTP hops; Security checks ignored .env, atomic writes, HTTPS and redacted errors. Do not display a real secret or token.'),
 ('5 min  /  interpret results','Ask whether a green configured indicator proves access. Compare saved configuration, mocked READY and an approved live READY result.')],
 'Before a live class check, pause projection for credential entry. Keep the session local if live access is not authorized. The API should expose a presence boolean, not the value; failure strings deserve the same redaction review as successful logs.',
 'Which hop failed?',
 'Learners distinguish token acquisition from the Responses request and label the proof as mock or live. Ask for a safe step name and timing, never raw credentials.',
 'An Entra error calls for a private config check; an agent 403 calls for role/endpoint review. At minute 55 switch to mocked tests rather than extending setup.',
 'The workshop role is Foundry Agent Consumer. Explain that authentication proves an identity; authorization determines whether that identity may use this agent. A successful mock cannot prove tenant provisioning.'),
 screen=('config',
 ('Read the configuration screen safely','FACILITATOR PROMPT','Which values identify the client, and which must never come back from GET?','Point to the secret field without revealing a value. Ask what a blank update should do.','Answer: tenant and client identify the registration; the secret stays server-side. Blank means preserve the stored value. The test log should show steps, not authorization headers.'),
 ('Check the configuration contract','IN THE DIALOG','Set the output folder to summaries. Save to .env before testing the connection.','View the connectivity log. Check that timings and reply are useful without exposing a secret or bearer token.','This is a reference screen, not evidence that your account is provisioned. If live access is unavailable, verify save, test and redaction with localhost mock endpoints and record that distinction.')),
 recap='Connection recap: storage, authentication and authorization are three different checks.'),

dict(short='Build a portable handoff',range='55–73',min=18,
 a=track('Build the summary as a background job',[
 ('Collect evidence in chronological order','Keep prompts, replies, recorded reasoning, tool outcomes, subagent results and file diffs. Use repo-relative paths; flag gaps instead of inventing history.'),
 ('Split only when the digest needs it','Bound long tool output while retaining errors. Summarize short digests once. For long ones, summarize each chunk, then synthesize the partial results.'),
 ('Wire the job into Session overview','Create session summary starts a job (202). Poll /api/summary/jobs/:jobId. Show phases, saved path, Copy summary, Download .md and View operation log.')],
 'POST /api/sessions/:id/summarize must return 400 CONFIG_REQUIRED when credentials are absent. Offer the config dialog instead of starting a doomed job. Preserve original sessions read-only and write the sanitized summary filename atomically.',
 'Can someone resume without your chat?',
 'Open summaries/<session-name>-summary.md. Find the objective, a relative changed path, a tool/test outcome and an ordered next step. Confirm the copied log is redacted.',
 'If config is missing, save settings first. If popups are blocked, use the inline log fallback. On failure, inspect the redacted phase and retry with a synthetic fixture.',
 'Use an approved synthetic fixture, not a personal workspace history. To prove the large-input branch, run a forced multi-chunk mock test and assert that map outputs feed one final synthesis. Record whether the result was live or mocked.'),
 p=track('Teach the handoff by asking someone to resume',[
 ('12 min  /  assign the build','Developer owns digest, job routes and UI. Tester forces multiple chunks with synthetic input. Security checks errors, download filenames and logs.'),
 ('6 min  /  demonstrate a job','Use a synthetic multi-turn session. Point to job phases rather than waiting silently. Open the log while running; inspect the saved Markdown when complete.'),
 ('Ask a cold reader to act','Give a partner only the handoff. Can they name the objective, the last verified change and the next action without an absolute machine path?') ],
 'Use the supplied “Verify the route migration” fixture: the transcript records that v1 and v2 passed, while the sample client update is still open. Does the handoff preserve that distinction? Mark opaque or unpersisted blocks unavailable; never invent the missing content.',
 'Accept a useful handoff, not a progress bar',
 'The cold reader finds a next step and supporting evidence. Tester shows both the one-pass path and forced map/synthesis path; Security checks the copied failure log.',
 'If live access stalls, stop retrying. Demonstrate the job contract with mocked results and label them. A blocked popup should reveal the inline viewer.',
 'If the output is generic, compare it to a known edit and test in the fixture. If the evidence never reached the digest, fix extraction before tuning the final prompt.'),
 screen=('log',
 ('Use the log to locate a stalled job','ASK THE ROOM','Which hop authenticated, and which returned the summary?','This is a real Chronicle job using mock Entra and Foundry responses, not a live connectivity check.','The viewer is a diagnostic surface, not proof of a useful summary. Inspect a synthetic failure as well as success. If a token is visible, stop sharing and remediate before retrying.'),
 ('Read and copy an operation log','LOCAL MOCK RUN','This real Chronicle job called mock Entra and Foundry endpoints. Trace the auth and response steps.','Test Copy log on synthetic data. If the popup is blocked, use the inline fallback; inspect redaction before sharing.','Open View operation log from the progress dialog or Session overview. A running job is polled for updates. Look for diagnostic information about the operation, not a dump of the session or configuration.')),
 diagram=('One pass or a map-and-synthesize job?','For a short session use MODE: FINAL_SESSION_SUMMARY once. For a long digest, label each SESSION_CHUNK_DIGEST with its part number; combine the partials into a final summary. Preserve chronology and uncertainty across boundaries.',None,
 'Ask: how would you prove the multi-chunk branch without a huge live request?',
 'Test with a small artificial chunk limit and assert that final synthesis receives every partial.'),
 recap='Handoff recap: preserve evidence, identify gaps and give the next person a first action.'),

dict(short='Verify the browser release',range='73–90',min=17,
 a=track('Release the browser app without a package install',[
 ('Generate and serve the icon','Copy appsample/build/render-icon.cjs into build/ unless already present. Run node build/render-icon.cjs. Copy build/icon.png to public/chronicle-icon.png.'),
 ('Prove the icon is real','Link /chronicle-icon.png as the favicon in public/index.html. In test/release-icon.test.js assert the link, HTTP 200, image/png and PNG signature.'),
 ('Run the final regression','Run node --check build/render-icon.cjs, node --test, then node --max-old-space-size=8192 src/server.js. Visit http://127.0.0.1:3210/.')],
 'Use an ephemeral loopback server, a temporary data directory and loadSamples: false in the release test. Preserve package.json, server routes, .env and all original histories. Test the static asset via HTTP, not merely by checking file existence.',
 'What did you actually release?',
 'A browser app: the icon loads locally, a synthetic conversation still opens, and Node tests pass. Review appsample/electron/main.mjs and preload.cjs read-only.',
 'If the tab icon is stale, open /chronicle-icon.png directly and try a fresh tab. If 3210 is busy, stop your old server or set PORT to 3211 and use that URL.',
 'The optional desktop host uses a sandboxed window, a utility process for the server and a narrow preload bridge for native pickers. No Electron launch, installer build or package manager belongs in this workshop. Stop your own server with Ctrl+C.'),
 p=track('Keep the release inside the browser boundary',[
 ('8 min  /  split the release work','Developer generates the PNG/ICO and wires the PNG favicon. Tester drafts a loopback HTTP check. Wait for the public asset before running the test.'),
 ('6 min  /  show the evidence','Open the icon URL directly, then a synthetic conversation. Ask for a green test run and a dependency-free manifest, not just a tab screenshot.'),
 ('3 min  /  compare the optional host','Read reference main.mjs and preload.cjs. Trace the sandboxed window, server utility process and narrow picker bridge. Do not launch or package Electron.')],
 'Documentation records how to start and test the browser app. Security reviews only the intended diff: local asset, HTML, renderer, test and README; no secrets or histories. Have learners stop their own servers at the end.',
 'Close at minute 90 with a release decision',
 'Ask for three proofs: a valid PNG over loopback HTTP, a conversation that still opens and a passing Node suite. Record separately whether Foundry was tested live.',
 'If only the icon looks wrong, test its direct URL before blaming the browser cache. Cut desktop discussion to one contrast: same UI, different host.',
 'Final prompt: “What would you hand to a teammate tomorrow?” Accept the portable Markdown and a reproducible test or release check, not credentials or raw sessions. The workshop ships no installer.'),
 screen=('finished',
 ('Inspect the finished browser surface','FINAL DEMO','Reopen a conversation first. A new summary action does not excuse a broken reader.','If approved access is available, summarize and open the log. Otherwise point to the mock test result and name its limit.','The finished screen illustrates the target surface. Do not mistake a reference capture for evidence from the participant’s run. Ask for the direct icon URL and an observed local test result.'),
 ('Compare the finished app with your build','BROWSER SMOKE TEST','Open a synthetic conversation. Confirm both the original reader and the new summary workflow remain reachable.','Try /chronicle-icon.png directly. Test an approved summary if available; otherwise record the local mock result only.','Compare actions, not pixels: browser themes and window widths can vary. Review the reference desktop architecture without running it; the release being verified is the browser release.')),
 recap='Release recap: ship the browser workflow; the desktop wrapper is a read-only comparison.')
]
